an “archive” label. The message remains in your mailbox, searchable and retrievable, and is not in Trash.\n- Delete: moves the message to your Trash/Deleted Items (or immediately permanently deletes, depending on settings). Messages in Trash are usually recoverable until you empty the Trash or until the provider’s retention period ends; after that they may be permanently removed.\n- Sync behavior: with IMAP (typical for modern email), archive/delete actions sync across devices. With POP, behavior depends on client settings (messages may be removed from server or left there).\n- Backups and server retention: even after you delete a message it may still exist in provider backups or logs for some time.\n\nConsequences & risks\n- Sender is unaffected and receives no notification.\n- Deleting is more likely to lead to permanent loss (after Trash retention ends). Archiving is safer if you may need the message later.\n- If you need to free storage, deleting (and then emptying Trash) reduces your storage quota; archiving usually does not free storage (it stays in your mailbox).\n\nIf you want provider-specific details or official citations, tell me which email service and confirm you want me to look them up. If you want me to perform a destructive action (delete/empty trash) in an account, I will first need the exact target and your explicit confirmation.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0668a9fef57c1509016a9a0aee553c87d08666ef51ece8d270","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"in_memory","reasoning":{"context":"current_turn","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","status":"completed","store":false,"temperature":1.0,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_to